## Writing a Job

Register jobs on the `Terse` app, then build a `TerseAgent` inside the handler with the prompt and skills you want the model to see:

```python
from terse_sdk import Terse
from terse_sdk.types.events import GithubPRTrigger
from terse_generated import GitHub, GitHubRepo, Slack, SlackChannel, TerseAgent

app = Terse()


@app.job(
    name="summarise-prs",
    triggers=[GitHub.on_pr(repo=GitHubRepo.Terse)],
)
def summarise_prs(event: GithubPRTrigger) -> None:
    agent = TerseAgent(
        prompt="You summarise pull requests.",
        skills=[
            GitHub.skill(repos=[GitHubRepo.Terse]),
            Slack.skill(channel=SlackChannel.AllTerseInc),
        ],
    )
    agent.run_and_wait(f"Summarise: {event.formatted_content}")
```

Skills control what the model can do during `agent.run()` / `agent.run_and_wait()`. If the skill also has deterministic tool wrappers (Slack, Attio, Snowflake), they are auto-attached on `agent.tools.*`:

```python
agent.tools.snowflake.execute_query(query="select 1")
agent.tools.slack.send_message(channel_id=SlackChannel.AllTerseInc.channel_id, message="hi")
```

`skills=[GitHub.skill(repos=[...])]` exposes repo-scoped GitHub tools to the model, but does not add deterministic `agent.tools.github.*` wrappers.
